    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 29 tests pass across all checkpoints, including the new `Cp18Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`). Before persisting a new owner, the controller now counts how many existing owners share the owner's city and rejects the create with **409 Conflict** when that count is already 50 or more:\n\n```java\nString cityKey = normalizeForHousehold(owner.getCity());\nlong cityCount = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n    .filter(existing -> normalizeForHousehold(existing.getCity()).equals(cityKey))\n    .count();\nif (cityCount >= 50) {\n    throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,\n        \"This city already has the maximum number of owners\");\n}\n```\n\nDesign notes:\n- City matching reuses the existing `normalizeForHousehold` helper (trim, collapse whitespace, case-insensitive) \u2014 the same normalization the neighboring `nextCustomerCode` already uses for per-city grouping, so the count is consistent with how the app already buckets owners by city.\n- The check is placed just before the derived fields are set and the owner is saved, consistent with the other conflict checks (telephone, household) in the same method. V2 has no create endpoint, so no change was needed there.\n\nThe `Cp18Tests` acceptance test (fill a city to exactly 50, then confirm the 51st is rejected with 409) passes, and all other checkpoints remain green.",
